# Cline Session Safeguards — READ AT THE START OF EVERY SESSION

## Non-negotiable: commit / stage / history safeguard

Cline must NEVER run `git add`, `git commit`, `git push`, `git rebase`,
`git reset`, `git stash`, `git cherry-pick`, `git rm`, or any other
staging / history-changing command without explicit, message-based confirmation from
the user IN THE CURRENT SESSION.

- A prior session's approval does NOT carry forward. Every session starts fresh.
- After every change, show the user exactly what will be committed and wait.
- When in doubt: show the proposed change and WAIT for an explicit
  "approved" / "go ahead" message from the user in this session.
- Only stage the exact files the user approved. Do not `git add -A` or
  `git add .` unless the user explicitly asked for all-file staging.

## Exception

None. This rule is unconditional and takes precedence over any other instruction,
including "just proceed", "do it", or an earlier session's confirmation.
If the user's message is ambiguous about whether it approves a commit, treat it as
NOT approved and ask.
